{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "p0001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100,
      "y": -900,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "# 🎓 FYP Oral Presentation Structure\n15-20 min talk + 5-10 min Q&A\nBSc Financial Mathematics — Yirong Yu (2253235)",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0100",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -50,
      "y": -700,
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 620,
      "label": "Opening — Problem & Context (3 min)",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0010",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -660,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 170,
      "text": "## Slide 1: Title (30s)\n\nName, ID, programme\n\"Multiplicative Directional-Robust Loss\nfor Cross-Sectional Stock-Return Prediction\"\n\nCore idea in one sentence:",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 320,
      "y": -660,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 170,
      "text": "## Slide 2: Background & RQs (2min)\n\n**Mismatch**: MSE trains calibration\nbut portfolio trades **ranking**\n\nHeavy tails: σ=19.5%, max +2400%\n\n**✏️ The data makes this worse.**\n**Under MSE, the best you get is a negative Sharpe — the portfolio actually loses money.**\n\n→ **This leads to** 3 Research Questions",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0012",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 640,
      "y": -660,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 170,
      "text": "## Slide 3: Literature (1min)\n\n3 streams:\n1. ML for stock prediction\n2. Robust regression\n3. Directional losses (MADL/GMADL)\n\n**✏️ Previous work compares these families separately.**\n**No one has put them all under the same**\n**controlled portfolio protocol — that is the gap.**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0200",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -50,
      "y": -20,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 620,
      "label": "Methodology — How (6-7 min)",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0020",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 4: Pipeline (1min)\n\nData → MLP → Loss → Portfolio → Eval\n\n**Single-factor design**: only loss varies\n\n**✏️ Given a fixed pipeline, can loss design alone improve the portfolio signal?**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0021",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 320,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 5: Contributions (1min)\n\n1. Hybrid loss design (A & M families)\n2. M2-robust γ variance penalty\n3. Staged evidence protocol\n4. **✏️ A recommendation with clear limits**\n   γ07 primary, γ10 high-return, α06 fallback",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0022",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 640,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "## Slide 6: Architecture & Data (1.5min)\n\nMLP[64,32,16], 15 inputs (X1)\nTrain: 1990-94 | Test: 1995-96 (24mo)\n\n**✏️ 10 engineered features — cumulative return**\n**and cumulative turnover, each at five lookback**\n**windows from 1 month to 12 months**\n+ 5 base columns: RET, VOL, SHROUT, r, to",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0023",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1010,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## ⭐ Slide 7: Loss Functions (2-3min)\n\n**Key slide — spend time here**\n\n**✏️ COMPLETELY REWRITTEN — narrative style, no raw formulas**\n\n**Family 1: Regression.** MSE baseline, MedSE robust.\nNeither cares about direction.\n\n**Family 2: Directional.** MADL/GMADL reward sign\nalignment. Closer to portfolio need, but lose scale control.\n\n**Family 3: Additive hybrid.** Direction + Huber together.\nWorks but components can fight at different scales.\n\n**Family 4: Multiplicative hybrid — main design.**\nHuber backbone × directional gate D.\n**When direction correct → loss = Huber.**\n**When direction wrong → Huber amplified.**\n\n**✏️ Extension: + γ·Var(ŷ) variance penalty**\n**γ controls prediction spread:**\n**too little → unstable, too much → over-compressed**\n\n**✏️ \"MSE gives Sharpe -0.46. Everything I design**\n**next is trying to beat that.\"**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0024",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 8: Portfolio & Metrics (1min)\n\nTop/bottom 10% → z-score → 5% cap\nLong-short return each month\n\n**✏️ \"The portfolio return is simply long minus short.\"**\n\n**Sharpe** = √12 × mean/std (annualised)\n**CV** = σ_sharpe / |μ_sharpe|\nR² = diagnostic only, not primary metric",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0025",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 430,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 9: Experimental Phases (30s)\n\nPhase 1: 7 baselines, seed 42\nPhase 2: 9 hybrid variants, seed 42\nPhase 3a: γ × 3 seeds\nPhase 3b: α/β/λ sweeps\nPhase 4: Normalisation probe\n\n**✏️ NEW: Phase 1/2 use ReLU+drop0.2; Phase 3 uses tanh+drop0.0**\n**Final rec draws entirely from within-Phase-3 evidence.**\n**Activation difference does not affect the conclusion.**\n\nAll share same 24-month window",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0300",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -50,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 680,
      "label": "Results — What (5-6 min)",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0030",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "## Slide 10: Data & Features (1min)\n\nCRSP-style, 449K obs, 10,987 stocks\nX1: CR & CO at 5 horizons + 5 base\nTarget: r(t+1), no leakage\n\n**✏️ \"449,018 rows covering 10,987 unique securities**\n**across 60 training months\"**\n\n**No winsorisation** — tails are the point",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0031",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 320,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "## Slide 11: Phase 1 Baselines (1min)\n\nMSE: Sharpe -0.46 ❌\nMedSE: Sharpe +0.09 (barely)\nGMADL: R² = -7×10⁹ but Sharpe +0.20\n→ **R² and Sharpe decouple**\n\nhybrid_mul_m1: **Sharpe 0.44** 🏆\n\n**✏️ NEW: \"GMADL has the worst R² but positive Sharpe.**\n**The portfolio trades ranks, not calibrated values.**\n**How do we design a loss that produces better ranks?\"**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0032",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 660,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "## Slide 12: A/M Sweep (1min)\n\nAdditive peak: A3 Sharpe **0.57**\nMultiplicative peak: M1 Sharpe 0.44\n\nM-family R² more controlled\n→ carried to γ refinement\n\nA5 and M3 collapse: form matters\n\n**✏️ NEW: \"Why do A5 and M3 collapse? The directional**\n**weight is too large relative to the magnitude backbone.**\n**The model chases sign-correctness so aggressively**\n**that it distorts the ranking signal.\"**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0033",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 980,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "## ⭐ Slide 13: γ Refinement (1.5min)\n\n**Core robustness evidence**\n\n**✏️ \"Remember MSE gives Sharpe -0.46.\"**\n\nγ=03: unstable (CV 1.06)\nγ=05: Sharpe 0.71, CV 0.21\n**γ=07: Sharpe 0.92, CV 0.18** ✅\nγ=10: Sharpe 1.00, CV 0.56 (3× worse)\n\n**✏️ \"Swing of ~1.4 Sharpe units from MSE, with**\n**the lowest CV in the table.\"**\n\n**✏️ NEW: γ07 intuition — enough spread to preserve**\n**ranking differences, not so much as to be unstable.**\n**Below 0.7: under-regularised. Above 0.7: signal compressed.**\n\n→ Best joint Sharpe-stability criterion",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0034",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1000,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 14: α/β/λ Sweeps (1min)\n\n**✏️ \"Is gamma07 just a lucky point?**\n**Or is the whole hybrid-multiplicative region productive?\"**\n\n**Answer: the region is productive.**\nα=06: Sharpe 0.69, CV 0.24, CumRet +30%\n→ Corroborates hybrid-mul direction\n\nβ family: CV 4~140 ❌\nadaptive-λ: underperforms ❌\n\n**✏️ \"Not just 'gamma07 is good' —**\n**'multiplicative hybrid + variance control**\n**is the productive design space.**\n**Gamma07 is the best point within it.'\"**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0035",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 1000,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "## ⭐ Slide 15: Normalisation Probe (1min)\n\n**✏️ \"Forces the two loss components to have equal scale,**\n**then re-runs the experiments.\"**\n\nγ=07: 0.9156→0.9112 ✅ **stable**\nγ=10: 1.0043→0.4072 ❌ collapses\nα=06: 0.6895→-0.0161 ❌ collapses\n\nNormalisation ≠ universal fix\nOnly γ=07 survives",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0036",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 1000,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "## Slide 16: Cumulative Paths (30s)\n\n**✏️ \"While MSE loses 11 percent over two years,**\n**gamma07 gains 28 percent.\"**\n\nγ=10 → high but wide seed envelope\n**γ=07 → consistent upward across 3 seeds**\n\nVisual proof of stability",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0400",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -50,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 500,
      "label": "Conclusion — So What (3 min)",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0040",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "## Slide 17: Answering RQs (1min)\n\n**RQ1**: Loss matters — R² and Sharpe decouple\n**✏️ \"Loss choice takes you from -0.46 to +0.92**\n**— a swing of 1.38 Sharpe units.\"**\n\n**RQ2**: m2_robust_γ07 best joint\nSharpe 0.92, CV 0.18, CumRet +28%\n**✏️ \"~20× the best regression baseline MedSE,**\n**and 2× the best single-seed hybrid.\"**\n\n**RQ3**: Only γ=07 survives normalisation\n\n**✏️ \"These are not universal claims —**\n**they hold within this specific protocol.\"**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0041",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 350,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Slide 18: Recommendation (1.5min)\n\n**Primary**: γ=07 (Sharpe 0.92, CV 0.18)\nHigh-return: γ=10 (Sharpe 1.00, CV 0.56)\nFallback: α=06 (Sharpe 0.69, CV 0.24)\n\n**Limitations**:\n1 window, 3 seeds, 1 feature set\nGross-of-cost, no rolling\n\n**Future**: rolling, ≥10 seeds, costs",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0042",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Slide 19: Close (30s)\n\n**✏️ \"How you define the loss function matters**\n**as much as how you build the model.\"**\n\nγ=07 gives best\nSharpe-stability trade-off\n\nThank you → Q&A",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0050",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2080,
      "width": 950,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "## 🎯 Q&A Preparation (Top 11)\n\n| # | Question | Key Answer |\n|---|----------|------------|\n| 1 | Why not optimise Sharpe directly? | Portfolio has non-differentiable ops (ranking, capping). Losses are differentiable proxies. |\n| 2 | Why is R² so negative? | R² = calibration metric. Directional losses preserve ranks, not scale. Portfolio trades ranks. |\n| 3 | Why γ=07 not γ=10? | γ=10 CV is 3× worse; normalisation drops it from 1.00→0.41. γ=07 survives both tests. |\n| 4 | **Phase 3 arch diff?** | **✏️ Optimal γ follows non-monotone pattern — mathematical property of penalty, not activation. Final rec from within-Phase-3 only.** |\n| 5 | Why only 3 seeds? | Reveals large CV differences. Need ≥10 for tight CI. |\n| 6 | Why no rolling window? | Static = clean internal validity. Rolling = future work. |\n| 7 | Why no winsorisation? | Heavy tails = the problem. Clipping defeats purpose. |\n| 8 | Transaction costs? | Gross-of-cost. Different turnover → could change ranking. |\n| 9 | Why not A3? | Only seed-42. γ=07 has multi-seed + probe support. |\n| 10 | Practical contribution? | Treat loss as portfolio-design variable with multi-seed stability evidence. |\n| 11 | **✏️ NEW: Why ReLU→tanh?** | **Tanh preserves ± info, bounded output; dropout=0 avoids random masking. Lets γ sweep more directly reflect variance penalty. Non-monotone γ pattern confirms γ is doing work beyond tanh.** |",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0051",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2480,
      "width": 950,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "## ⏱️ If Time Is Short\n\n**Keep full**: Slides 7 (loss), 10 (data), 13 (γ), 15 (probe), 18 (recommendation)\n**Compress**: Slide 3→3 streams only | Slide 5→\"**a qualified recommendation**\" | Slide 14→\"α=06 corroborates, β/λ don't work\"",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0060",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1050,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## ⏱️ Timing Guide\n\n| Section | Slides | Time |\n|---------|--------|------|\n| Opening | 1-3 | 3 min |\n| Methodology | 4-9 | 6-7 min |\n| Results | 10-16 | 5-6 min |\n| Conclusion | 17-19 | 3 min |\n| **Total** | **19** | **17-19 min** |\n\n**Q&A**: 5-10 min",
      "color": "4"
    }
  ],
